ide of Uyama's face was shrouded in unprecedented sorrow. [2603] Epilogue\n[2604] The next morning, Uyama disappeared from the room next door. [2605] Not only did she disappear, but her luggage and Shanke's luggage were also gone without a trace. All that remained in the room were the daily items that were already there. The cold and distant atmosphere filled the room, just like the first day they arrived. [2606] Yuying had left... Jingma couldn't help but accept the fact, even though he didn't want to. She had left early in the morning without telling anyone, leaving Jingma alone. [2607] It wasn't completely incomprehensible. Yuying's face, gazing at the burning Yushe, had shown something other than the sense of accomplishment in solving the case, the satisfaction of avenging her father, the exhaustion of thinking the case was solved, or the regret of causing everything to disappear. She was ashamed. [2608] Yuying gazed at the dancing flames, her face full of sorrow. Initially, Jingma had thought it might be sympathy for Yushi, but now he realized it was shame. She pitied herself for being unable to see clearly and felt deeply ashamed of it. [2609] As a woman, the case took longer to solve... Yuying had also expressed her disappointment in this regard, didn't she? For a woman, it was difficult to believe that a mother would calmly kill her child to deal with a difficult situation. But Yuying seemed to have reached a conclusion - because she was a woman, her eyes were blinded. [2610] To be a detective, one must abandon one's identity as a woman, and Jingma, as a man, became an obstacle. It was clear as day. But Jingma still thought that this case could be their first step, and that he could walk hand in hand with Yuying in the future. Perhaps he could become a spiritual support for Yuying, just like Shank was for Yuying's mother. He was indulging himself in his fantasies...\n[2611] What was that night's union? Shin'ichi stood motionless, staring at his hands. The feeling of embracing Yuri, Yuri's warmth, still vivid in his memory. Was it all a dream? Was it just his own feeling that not only his body but also his heart had fused together? Was it all an illusion? Shin'ichi hugged his head and crouched down, just like the day he killed his father after hearing his confession. [2612] ...No, there was one thing that was certain. Yuri didn't need Shin'ichi. It was Shin'ichi who needed Yuri, to survive, to find a reason to survive, he needed Yuri. [2613] Shin'ichi stood up with vacant eyes, staggering back to his room, and began to quietly pack his things. [2614] ...and finally, there was one thing that was certain. Yuri didn't need Shin'ichi. It was Shin'ichi who needed Yuri, to survive, to find a reason to survive, he needed Yuri. [2615] Shin'ichi stood up with vacant eyes, staggering back to his room, and began to quietly pack his things. [2616] For Jingma, there was no other choice. [2617] Second Part: Winter 2003\n[2618] 2\n[2619] 1\n[2620] As Jingma walked along the concrete path, he saw the signboard of Qinai Tang hanging in front of him, and for a moment, memories from eighteen years ago revived in his heart. All the experiences he had then, along with the deep longing, resurfaced in his mind. [2621] Only a year ago, Shibazaki didn't know who he was. He woke up in a hospital bed, having lost all his memories. It was a man named Higashiyama who found him, and since then, he has been living as Higashiyama Harumi. [2622] However, now the situation has been clarified. Ten days after the murder in the winter of 18 years ago, Shibazaki committed suicide. He left the village of Kibaeki, wanting to die in a place completely unrelated to it. So, he slit his wrists in a valley in Kagoshima and threw himself into the water. Like the Dragon's Pond, the place had romantic legends. It was said that more than ten people came to commit suicide there every year. [2623] However, whether it was fortunate or unfortunate, Shibazaki was found hanging on the shore, on the verge of death, by the villagers. He was taken to the hospital and saved. Later, Shibazaki found out that there were two small waterfalls between the place where he committed suicide and the place where he was found. Perhaps he suffered a head injury then, or he may have lost too much blood and gone into shock, affecting the hippocampus. The exact reason remains unknown, but Shibazaki lost all his memories. [2624] Moreover, to prevent anyone from investigating him after his death, Shibazaki disposed of all items that could identify him. As a result, he didn't even know who he was or where he came from. There are countless missing persons in the world, and Shibazaki's disappearance would not have been reported, making it natural for his identity to remain unknown. Lying on the hospital bed, Shibazaki was a pitiful man who had lost everything, attempted suicide, and failed to die. [2625] After a year of rehabilitation, Shibazaki accepted Higashiyama's kindness and began working on Higashiyama's farm under the name Higashiyama Harumi. Shibazaki was found by the river, and Harumi was the name of the river. Shibazaki quickly learned his job and, since he had no past, he devoted himself to his work. As time passed, he gained Higashiyama's trust and is now appointed as the supervisor of the labor site. During his hospital stay, he spent every night worrying about who he was and why he had committed suicide. However, as he spent more time on the farm, he gradually stopped caring. Perhaps it was also because the farm work was so busy that there was no time for introspection. [2626] Kei Mori's memories were revived a year ago. At that time, a travel program introducing the village of Kibe appeared on Kei Mori's screen. The program was only fifteen minutes long, and the images of the Kibe River and the Dragon's Head were clearly displayed, just as they were in the past. [2627] The feeling Kei Mori had at that time is unforgettable. It was like millions of insects spreading from the spinal cord to the whole body, causing goosebumps, like an alien breaking through the muscles and skin and about to break through the body. Then, the next second, the dam of the memories buried for seventeen years collapsed. It was that simple. [2628] Kei Mori knew he was Kei Mori, the farmer. [2629] Kei Mori told Hayato about his recovered memories, and Hayato was happy for him but asked him what he planned to do next. Kei Mori chose to stay on the farm and continue living as Dayou Higorou, just as he had been doing for these years. [2630] And Kei Mori is standing in front of the Kibe River now, for a reason. A week ago, the Dragon's Head was washed away by heavy rain. [2631] Although he had decided to abandon Jinten Jinma and live as Dayo Sanjuro, the case of the Kikuzuki family and, of course, the most important thing, Oyama, remained in the corner of his mind. No, not just residual, he deliberately preserved it. It was no longer possible to meet, but the man named Jinten Jinma had existed, as a kind of bittersweet memory, preserved in his heart. So the collapse of the dragon's head was like a thin chain connecting the past, causing him great shock. [2632] Jinma broke the seal and investigated Oyama on the internet. Oyama had become a famous detective in urban legends online. Although she was completely absent from the mainstream media, she became a topic on the internet through word of mouth from people involved in the case. Among them were several terrible crimes that Jinma had heard about in news reports, and each case was reported as \"the police quickly solved the case.\" [2633] Oyama achieved great success as a detective, and abandoning her was not without value... Jinma was satisfied and wanted to close the window. If everything had ended there, Jinma would not have come to Kikuzuki village now. [2634] However, the next page reported Oyama's death. Six months ago, a murder case occurred in Kamisu, Chiba. During the investigation, Oyama was taken away by the desperate killer, and her whereabouts were unknown. A month later, the bodies of Oyama and the killer were found floating in Miraji Bay. Eighteen years ago, Oyama survived the fiery madness of Kikuzuki, but this time she lost her life. [2635] That day, Jinma cried. She was only thirty-five years old. His sorrow and regret could not be stopped. So he decided to go to the Kikuzuki Dragon, to the place where he and Oyama first met. Before his memories faded completely, he wanted to go there once more, to pray for Oyama's peace at the Dragon's Pond. [2636] A small incident occurred in a remote rural area, and the news about the incident happened to catch Jouma's eye. Perhaps this event itself was the work of the gods. In any case, Jouma took a leave of absence and came to this village. [2637] \"Are you the Mr. Jou who made the reservation?\" [2638] With the familiar voice, the figure of Juko appeared. His face had gained a few wrinkles, making him feel the passage of time, but his physique was still robust. Eighteen years have passed, and he should be close to fifty years old. [2639] Juko seemed not to notice that Jouma had come, but Jouma's voice made him react, and he stared intently at Jouma. [2640] \"...Is it Kita-san?\" [2641] Indeed, Jingma replied honestly. In Kumo's eyes, what kind of image did he have? He had been wavering between life and death for a long time, and his face should have appeared more deeply etched with the marks of time than Kumo's. [2642] \"It's really you, isn't it? How have you been? And why did you change your name to Nishikata-san?\" [2643] Kumo asked, looking quite surprised. [2644] \"I came here because I heard the news of the collapse of the Dragon's Head. As for this name... I just wanted to surprise you. If you feel offended, I apologize.\" [2645] There was no need to force the matter of amnesia. [2646] Jumo believed him sincerely and gently waved his hand, saying, \"It's nothing. I was really surprised. I thought you wouldn't come back after such a case. You still care about this village, after all these years... Over the years, the village has undergone various changes.\" [2647] By the end, Jumo's voice had grown softer, and he looked a little melancholy. [2648] \"I shouldn't have come. It seems I've reminded you of the past.\" [2649] \"How could that be? It's been a long time since we last saw each other, and I'm really glad to see you again. Come in, I'll make you a nice dinner tonight.\" [2650] Jumo invited Jumo into the room and poured him some green tea while telling him about the events of the past few years. [2651] The following spring, after the murder, Shima's daughter Shizuka obediently inherited the family tradition and has continued it to this day. She married Detective Sasori and gave birth to triplets. [2652] \"Triplets... Just like the Shizuka sisters.\" [2653] The tragic memories flashed back in Shima's mind, recalling the tragic fate of the three sisters who didn't survive. [2654] \"That's right.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 2:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:48 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nThe fence separating the courtyard from the house had been changed to a clay wall five years ago. However, the peaceful scenery with the mountains behind it remained intact, and the carp in the pond jumped happily, probably having been replaced. [3265] On the west side of the pond where the shrine used to be, several tulip trees, dogwood trees, and Chinese chestnut trees were planted in a checkerboard pattern. These trees surrounded a grassy area the size of a sumo wrestling ring, with a monument in the center. [3266] The stele was about two meters high and shaped like a long chess piece. The top end was carved with the family crest of the Qin family. After walking around the stele, it was found that there was no inscription on the front and back. It