ression becomes serious again: \"I have somewhat eased my feelings towards my mother-in-law, but I will never forgive my father. Betraying a sick mother with an affair is unforgivable. And he didn't seem to regret it either, as if he had another woman outside.\u201d\n[3312] Ando does not hide his disgust and harshly condemns his father. Because he is a relative, because he has blood ties, hatred becomes even deeper, and Shiro understands this too well. [3313] \"So he's not like the previous Teng-san, someone who wants to gain influence in the Ichijo family with ambition?\" Oyama takes advantage of the right moment to ask again. [3314] \"Only my father-in-law can I say is not that kind of person. He cooperated with my father and grandfather, and made Auntie Menaka regret deeply.\" [3315] For Shiro, who has seen how Auntie Menaka treated Oyama, this is a small piece of news that can make his heart happy. [3316] Later, Yuying repeated the question he had asked others, but without any new gains. After asking, it was Heshang's turn to ask, and the object was Jingma. [3317] \"By the way, what happened to Mr. Zhong after that incident? You seem to have left with Miss Yuying.\" [3318] Jingma's old wounds were pricked. [3319] \"Me? The assistant's position was dismissed without saying a word, and I'm not good at this job anyway. Later, I went back to Tokyo and lived a normal life. Eighteen years have passed, and both Tokyo and this Qiegou village have changed a lot, but I haven't changed at all, and I'm still single.\" [3320] \"Is that so. Miss Yuying and Mr. Zhong looked very good together, so I wondered what was going on. Well, I really didn't care about it at the time, but I thought about it later. However, the impression you gave then and now is very different. At that time, you seemed to be forced by something, and there were some scary places.\" [3321] Hidemasa probed Shizuka's wounds, although he himself was unaware of it. At that time, Shizuka was at the point of committing suicide, and \"being pushed to the limit\" was indeed the case, but he was embarrassed that even strangers could see through it. [3322] \"Well, everyone goes through various things in life. And I seem more stable now only because I'm getting older and my skin is sagging. I'm almost forty years old. In my opinion, you've also matured a lot.\" [3323] \"Is that so. Mr. Kindaichi is now a kind and approachable person. Ah, I'm sorry for saying such an informal thing.\" [3324] \"It's okay. My school friends used to say the same thing about me.\" [3325] Of course, this was a lie. There was no one who knew Shizuka's past except for the members of the Kagiyama family. [3326] In this sense, the Kubota family can be said to be the only link between Shima and his past, the place where he lived eighteen years ago, despite the fact that he was suffering from despair at that time. [3327] \"I'll be leaving now. It's time for my shift.\" [3328] Andou looked at his watch and bowed lightly to the two of them before turning and leaving. After his figure disappeared, Oyim asked Shima, \"Mr. Shima, how have you been for the past eighteen years?\" [3329] \"What's wrong? Even Oyim is asking about this now?\" [3330] Oyim's expression was as serious as when he was investigating, and Shima couldn't help but shrink back. [3331] \"I heard from Detective Sato that you've been missing for the past eighteen years. I asked Detective Sato to wait while I questioned you on behalf of the police.\" [3332] Since they had investigated the situation with Inoue, it was only natural to investigate Keiichiro's past as well. Keiichiro had momentarily forgotten this aspect. [3333] \"Oyama must know about my family situation as well.\" [3334] Oyama nods silently. [3335] \"So after that case, I gave up on myself because I felt empty. Since then, I've been living with Mr. Higashiyama in Miyazaki. Now, I'm living as Higashiyama Keijiro. I'll give you my contact information later, so please have the police 